<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73168" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁλκ-ός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>drawing to oneself, attractive,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θερμόν τε καὶ ὁ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					931a25
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάθημα ψυχῆς ὁλκὸν ἀπὸ τοῦ
					γιγνομένου ἐπὶ τὸ ὄν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					521d
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁλκὸν . . ψυχῆς πρὸς
			ἀλήθειαν</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				527b
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁλκοτέρας τὰς ῥίζας ποιεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>CP</u>
					3.17.3
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑλκοτέρας</span> cod. A: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑλκτικωτέρας</span> Wimmer). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>trailing,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁλκὰ βαίνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hld.
					10.30
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ότερον</span>”
				<i>slowly,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					3.5
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>possible,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁλκά: δυνατά,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>liable to be attracted, having a propensity,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. διάνοιαι παρθένων πρὸς ἀρετήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.229
				</span></i>
			.</div>
